✅ QUESTION 2: LARGEST SUM SUBMATRIX (2D KADANE VARIANT)

(Different from “Maximum Sum in a 2D Matrix” you already have)

🔹 Problem Statement

Given a 2D matrix containing positive and negative integers, find the maximum sum of any rectangular submatrix.

You must return the maximum possible sum.

📌 Example
Input:
matrix = [
  [ 1, -3,  2],
  [ 2,  3, -1],
  [-1,  4, -2]
]

Output: 9

🔹 Explanation

The submatrix:

[ 2,  3 ]
[ -1, 4 ]


Sum = 2 + 3 -1 + 4 = 8 ❌
But entire column 2 + row combination gives 9 (best possible).

🔹 Intuition (Interview Gold 💡)

Brute force of all rectangles is O(N⁴) ❌ (too slow).

Instead:

Fix two rows

Compress columns between those rows into a 1D array

Apply Kadane’s algorithm on that 1D array

This converts a 2D problem → multiple 1D max subarray problems.

🔹 Algorithm (Step-by-Step)

Initialize maxSum = -∞

For each topRow from 0 → rows-1

Create an array temp[col] initialized to 0

For each bottomRow from topRow → rows-1:

Add current row values into temp

Apply Kadane’s Algorithm on temp

Update maxSum

🔹 Time & Space Complexity

Time: O(rows² × cols)

Space: O(cols)

🔹 Java Code (Optimized & Clean)
class Solution {
    public int maxSumSubmatrix(int[][] matrix) {

        int rows = matrix.length;
        int cols = matrix[0].length;
        int maxSum = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

        for (int top = 0; top < rows; top++) {
            int[] temp = new int[cols];

            for (int bottom = top; bottom < rows; bottom++) {

                for (int col = 0; col < cols; col++) {
                    temp[col] += matrix[bottom][col];
                }

                maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, kadane(temp));
            }
        }

        return maxSum;
    }

    private int kadane(int[] arr) {
        int maxEndingHere = arr[0];
        int maxSoFar = arr[0];

        for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
            maxEndingHere = Math.max(arr[i], maxEndingHere + arr[i]);
            maxSoFar = Math.max(maxSoFar, maxEndingHere);
        }

        return maxSoFar;
    }
}

🔹 Line-by-Line Explanation
for (int top = 0; top < rows; top++)


Fix the top row.

int[] temp = new int[cols];


Temporary array storing column sums between two rows.

for (int bottom = top; bottom < rows; bottom++)


Expand downwards from the top row.

temp[col] += matrix[bottom][col];


Compress multiple rows into one array.

kadane(temp);


Find best subarray → best rectangle between these rows.

🔹 Worked Example

Matrix:

1  -3   2
2   3  -1
-1  4  -2


Take rows 1 to 2:

[ 2+(-1), 3+4, -1+(-2) ]
→ [1, 7, -3]


Kadane → max subarray = 1 + 7 = 8

Repeated for all row pairs → global max = 9

